PHP 8.6 keeps the language scanner globals in native thread-local storage
and has shared extensions reference that variable directly. Mach-O cannot
do that: shared extensions link with -undefined dynamic_lookup, and ld
rejects a thread-local reference to a symbol it cannot see ("illegal
thread local variable reference to regular symbol
_language_scanner_globals"), which breaks ext/tokenizer in ZTS builds.

Take the route Windows already takes for the same reason: a shared
extension reaches the scanner globals through language_scanner_globals_id.
The core keeps the direct thread-local access.

--- a/Zend/zend_globals_macros.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_globals_macros.h
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 /* Language Scanner */
 #ifdef ZTS
 extern ZEND_API ts_rsrc_id language_scanner_globals_id;
-# if defined(ZEND_WIN32) && !defined(LIBZEND_EXPORTS)
+# if (defined(ZEND_WIN32) && !defined(LIBZEND_EXPORTS)) || (defined(__APPLE__) && defined(ZEND_COMPILE_DL_EXT))
 # define LANG_SCNG(v) TSRMG(language_scanner_globals_id, zend_php_scanner_globals *, v)
 # else
 #  ifdef ZEND_WIN32
